# Deploy to GitHub (anchormyfinances1)

## Canonical remote

- **Repository**: `https://github.com/faisuseng3-dotcom/anchormyfinances1.git`
- **Remote name**: `origin`
- **Default branch**: `main`

When the user asks to deploy, release, or push to GitHub, treat that as **shipping committed code to `origin/main`** unless they name another branch or remote.

## Agent workflow

1. Confirm `origin` points at the URL above (`git remote -v`). If it differs, set it with:
   - `git remote set-url origin https://github.com/faisuseng3-dotcom/anchormyfinances1.git`
2. Ensure changes are committed (`git status`). Stage and commit when there are uncommitted changes the user wants included; use clear commit messages.
3. Before pushing substantive feature or fix work, run quality checks when reasonable: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run build` (fix failures or report them).
4. Push: `git push -u origin main` (or the branch the user requested).

## Notes

- Authentication (HTTPS token, SSH, or GitHub CLI) is handled on the machine running git; do not embed secrets in the repo or rules.
- If push fails (auth, protected branch, conflicts), report the error and the next concrete step (e.g. pull/rebase, fix CI, open PR).
